Activity 1: Tutorial Points Web Browsers
In the Tutorial Points Web Browsers activity I learned about the fundamentals of web browsers and how they
function as application software that allows users to access and interact with websites on the internet.
The topic focused on browser architecture, including the controller, interpreter and client program components 
that work together to process user input and display web content. I also learned how browsers connect to web servers 
using protocols such as HTTPS and how features like bookmarks, favorites, hyperlinks and saved web elements improve user efficiency.
This activity helped me understand that web browsers are tools for communication, research and information access.
In my future environment I can apply this knowledge by using web browsers more effectively when conducting online research managing information
and maintaining secure internet browsing habits for personal, educational and professional purposes.
Activity 2: Comparing Brave, Chrome and Edge Browsers
In the Compare Brave, Chrome and Edge Browsers activity I learned about the features, strengths and limitations of different web browsers.
Brave emphasized privacy, security, ad blocking, faster page loading and reduced data usage.
Chrome offered compatibility, AI-powered features, synchronization across devices and support for extensions
although it may experience privacy concerns and performance issues. Microsoft Edge provided productivity tools, 
page summarization, personalization and assistance with completing tasks. By comparing these web browsers 
I learned that each web browser serves user needs and priorities. I can apply this knowledge in my environment by selecting the web browser
that best matches my goals. For example I may use Brave when privacy is important Chrome when I need compatibility with Google services and Edge
when I want productivity features that help with school or work tasks.
Activity 3: Practicing Web Browsers on macOS
In the Practice Using Web Browsers on macOS activity I learned how Safari and other web browsers can be customized to improve accessibility and productivity. 
The topic focused on features such, as the Smart Search field, homepage settings, bookmarks, tabs, search engines and browsing preferences. 
I learned that organizing bookmarks and customizing browser settings can save time and make navigation more efficient. This activity showed me the importance of personalizing technology to meet needs and preferences. In my future environment I can apply this knowledge by organizing websites that I frequently use for school, work, banking and communication. Using bookmarks, tabs and customized settings will help me work efficiently stay organized and quickly access important online resources.
